From u70902530ae69f613 at groups.google.com  Fri Nov  2 10:34:29 2018
From: u70902530ae69f613 at groups.google.com (Noppol Kobmoo)
Date: Fri, 02 Nov 2018 10:34:29 +0000
Subject: Annotate a list of trees with user annotations
Message-ID: <RwPGsLMtIuQ.xq1Cfy0KCwAJ@bioc-ggtree.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/bioc-ggtree/c/RwPGsLMtIuQ/m/xq1Cfy0KCwAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hi,

I have a list of trees, stored under a multiphylo object. Each tree is from different part of the genome and all trees have the same taxa, thus tip names.
What I would like to do is to color the tips of my trees according to an external annotation.
I know that ggtree has %<+% that allow attaching an annotation to a tree. Is there a way to work around to make this work with a multiphylo object so that I can visualize them all at once with facet_wrap. Otherwise, I will have to do this one by one and assembling them à posteriori, which will require much more manipulation.

Thank you very much in advance.

From ucec41188340e8212 at groups.google.com  Sun Nov  4 09:26:01 2018
From: ucec41188340e8212 at groups.google.com (Yu, Guangchuang)
Date: Sun, 04 Nov 2018 09:26:01 +0000
Subject: Re: Annotate a list of trees with user annotations
Message-ID: <RwPGsLMtIuQ.CFnR9GtPCAAJ@bioc-ggtree.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <RwPGsLMtIuQ.xq1Cfy0KCwAJ@bioc-ggtree.groups.google.com>
References: <RwPGsLMtIuQ.xq1Cfy0KCwAJ@bioc-ggtree.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/bioc-ggtree/c/RwPGsLMtIuQ/m/CFnR9GtPCAAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

In this case, you don’t need to attach external data to the tree object.

Just visualize the tree and color the tip by tip label, than use scale_color_manual to set the colors.

